					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-03-17 | Saturday</font></strong><br><br>watt it is, folkers.<br /><br />big up to <strong>Big Rob Milliron</strong> for organizing the 2nd installment of the <strong>PUSH MC Battle</strong> last nite.  it was an entertaining event that was judged by <strong>Jake One</strong>, <strong>Larry Mizzel, Jr</strong>., and myself.  what made this battle unique from the other ones that i&#39;ve been to in the town was the judging format.  the two MCs would go at it for two 1-minute rounds, and then the attention would be focused on the judges for an American Idol style critique.  folks would sometimes say that it was really the judges who won the battle cuz they had the best punchlines.<br /><br />one of the better lines from the MCs that evening was:<br /><br /><em>&quot;this dood is wearin Air BumFights&quot;</em><br /><br />and from the judges:<br /><br /><em>&quot;that sounded like a bunch of drunken fraternity rap.&quot;<br /><br />&quot;MC1 here has a better flow, better delivery, and much filthier voice... but since this is a battle, which has more to do with capping and jokes, i&#39;m gonna have to give it to MC2 even tho (*turns to MC2) homie, your flow is worse, your delivery is bad, and you straight up have a wack voice.  i&#39;d never buy your record.  but hey, you got jokes.&quot;</em><br /><br /><u><strong>national tv cameo</strong></u><br />speaking of <strong>American Idol</strong>, people keep hittin us up to talk about how <strong>Blake Lewis</strong> mentioned MASSLINE supergroup <strong>Common Market</strong> on national television earlier this week when he was asked what music he listens to.<br /><object width="425" height="350" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" data="http://www.youtube.com/v/ugVBSXi1PU4"><br /><param name="movie" value="http://www.youtube.com/v/ugVBSXi1PU4"></param><br /><param name="wmode" value="transparent"></param><br /></object><br />yes yes, we know.  yes yes, we know that guy--you can talk to him in the forums by clicking <a href="../smf/index.php?board=2.0"><strong>here</strong></a>.<br /><br /><u><strong>love is work</strong></u><br /><strong>Gabriel Teodros</strong> continues to garner good press for his solo effort, <strong>Lovework</strong>.  you can peep his interview on <strong>NPR</strong> <a href="http://www.npr.org/templates/story/story.php?storyId=7853032"><strong><u>here</u></strong></a>, and read his review in <strong>Rolling Stone</strong> <u><a href="http://www.rollingstone.com/reviews/album/13067171/review/13711412/lovework"><strong>here</strong></a></u>.  Lovework was just recently added to <strong>KCRW</strong> outta LA as well which, word has it, rarely adds any hip hop to their rotation.  do yo&#39; thing gabe!  (and your thing too leeore, haha.)<br /><br />that&#39;s it for now tho.  stay tuned and join us in the forums.<br /><br />saba<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-03-16 | Friday</font></strong><br><br><strong><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial">STOP
THE KILLINGS in the PHILIPPINES</span></strong>

<p><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial">The
nationwide <span style="font-weight: bold">Stop the Killings tour</span> organized by <strong>BAYAN-USA </strong>and <strong>Geologic
</strong>of <span style="font-weight: bold">Blue Scholars</span> ends in Seattle on March 23, 2007. Since 2001, over <strong>835
</strong>activists of BAYAN member organizations and progressive party lists like
Bayan Muna have been <strong>assassinated </strong>or forced to &quot;<strong>disappear</strong>&quot;.
The national Stop the Killings tour was organized to raise consciousness around
the killing of progressives and to raise money to support travel expenses for
the families of victims to testify at Permanent Peoples Tribunal at the Hague.</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial">The
show is to inspire active participation in finding and defending Justice and
Peace in Seattle, the Philippines, Iraq and the world.</span></p><br /><p><span style="text-decoration: underline; font-weight: bold">
Media coverage and informational links:</span><br />
Seattle P-I: <a href="http://seattlepi.nwsource.com/national/1153AP_US_Philippines_Killings.html?source=rss" target="_blank" onclick="return top.js.OpenExtLink(window,event,this)">Click here</a> (3/13/07)<br />
Yahoo! News: <a href="http://news.yahoo.com/s/nm/20070314/pl_nm/philippines_usa_killings_dc_1" target="_blank" onclick="return top.js.OpenExtLink(window,event,this)">Click here</a> (3/14/07)<br />
Senate Hearing Testimony: <a href="http://www.amnestyusa.org/news/document.do?id=ENGUSA20070314001" target="_blank" onclick="return top.js.OpenExtLink(window,event,this)">Click here</a> (3/14/07)<br />
