Anakbayan Seattle: <a href="http://myspace.com/anakbayanseattle" target="_blank" onclick="return top.js.OpenExtLink(window,event,this)">Click here</a><br />The Vera Project: <a href="http://theveraproject.org/" target="_blank" onclick="return top.js.OpenExtLink(window,event,this)">




Click here</a></p><p><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial"><span style="font-weight: bold"><span style="font-family: arial,sans-serif"><span style="color: #3333ff">





Stop the Killings Tour 2007 - Seattle</span></span><br /><span style="font-family: arial,sans-serif; color: #3333ff">
Friday, March 23</span><br /><span style="font-family: arial,sans-serif; color: #3333ff">
The Vera
Project&nbsp; (Corner of Warren &amp; Republican at the Seattle Center)</span><br /><span style="font-family: arial,sans-serif; color: #3333ff">
7:30pm, ALL AGES</span><br />
<span style="font-weight: bold"><span style="font-weight: bold; font-family: arial,sans-serif; color: #3333ff">$10 donation</span><br />
</span></span></span>
</p><p><span style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial"><span style="font-weight: bold"><span style="font-family: arial,sans-serif">Featuring</span></span><span style="font-family: arial,sans-serif">





: Prometheus Brown (aka Geologic of </span><a style="font-weight: bold; font-family: arial,sans-serif" href="http://bluescholars.com/" target="_blank" onclick="return top.js.OpenExtLink(window,event,this)">
Blue Scholars</a><span style="font-family: arial,sans-serif">),
Kiwi of the </span><a style="font-weight: bold; font-family: arial,sans-serif" href="http://nativeguns.com/" target="_blank" onclick="return top.js.OpenExtLink(window,event,this)">Native Guns</a><span style="font-family: arial,sans-serif">





, Rogue Pinay, Bridget Hermano, Dax, El Dia, DJ Daps1 and much more!</span></span></p><span style="font-weight: bold"><span style="font-weight: bold"><font size="2" style="font-family: arial,sans-serif">Purchase tickets online!<br /><a href="http://www.brownpapertickets.com/event/13258" target="_blank" onclick="return top.js.OpenExtLink(window,event,this)"><span style="font-weight: bold">http://www.brownpapertickets.com/event/13258</span></a><span style="font-weight: bold">




<br /></span></font></span></span><p>If you cannot make this event but would like to donate or sponsor a
youth to attend this show (minimum $10 donation), please make checks
out to &quot;<span style="font-weight: bold">Anakbayan Seattle</span>&quot; and mail them to:
</p><span style="color: #3333ff; font-weight: bold">Anakbayan Seattle
</span><br /><span style="color: #3333ff; font-weight: bold">3815 Othello St. Suite 100 #138</span><div style="color: #3333ff; font-weight: bold">
</div><div style="text-align: left"><span style="color: #3333ff; font-weight: bold">Seattle, WA 98118</span></div><p>&nbsp;</p><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-03-14 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br><u><strong>Students, Youth, Soldiers (and those in Solidarity!)</strong></u><br /><p><!--[endif]-->Join the Troops Home Now Coalition to Kiss the War Goodbye!</p><p style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt">&nbsp;</p>Featuring local hip-hop artist:<br /><strong>Massline Media&#39;s Gabriel Teodros </strong><br /><br /><p style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt">&nbsp;</p><strong>Monday, March 19th, 2007</strong><br />Westlake, 4th and Pine &ndash; Downtown Seattle<br /><br />3:00pm - Hip Hop Artist <strong>Gabriel Teodros</strong>, Speakers and Spoken Word.<br /><p>4:00pm - March to the <strong>Federal Building</strong>.  Bring signs and friends!</p><p>4:30pm - Join in protest at Federal Building with other anti-war groups</p><em>Sponsored by Troops Home Now Coalition</em><br /><br /><p><u><strong>Contact:</strong></u></p><p><strong>Carrie Hathorn</strong>, 206-963-4873, <a href="mailto:calni27@gmail.com" target="_blank" onclick="return top.js.OpenExtLink(window,event,this)">calni27@gmail.com</a></p><p style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt">&nbsp;</p>Download flyers at <a href="http://www.troopshomenowcoalition.org/" target="_blank" onclick="return top.js.OpenExtLink(window,event,this)">www.troopshomenowcoalition.org</a><br /><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-03-13 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br>Another big Massline announcement is coming. Soon.<br />
<br />
But for now, all you get is an update from me (Geo), sipping the sexy
beast at the airport en route to Chicago (tonight!), Milwaukee
(tomorrow) and New York (Friday, 3/16) for the second half of the <strong>Stop the Killings Tour</strong> reppin my <strong>Bayan-USA</strong>
shirt. It&#39;s getting heavy back in the PI with the government&#39;s attempts
to crack down on the progressive movement. I&#39;ll be heading out solo for
this half of the trip (<strong>Kiwi</strong> will be holding it down back in the West... but will be in town for the Seattle show 3/23!).<br />
<br />
Tonight I&#39;ll be making a return to <strong>Subterranean</strong>, where my
peoples The Pacifics have been holding down the longest-running hip-hop
weekly in the Windy City. It&#39;s been a minute since I&#39;ve been back, and
it&#39;s only fitting that I break bread with the folks who put me on when
I was just getting started with this rap shit.<br />
<br />
<strong>Blue Scholars</strong> will always have a connection with Chicago - our first two shows happened when The Pacifics, <strong>Typical Cats</strong> &amp; <strong>Primeridian</strong>
let us open up for their tour back in &#39;02. Before working with Sabzi, I
was working producers Bay Root Productions, who provided beats for
Pacifics&#39; first album. Through the <em>isangmahal-Yellowtech</em> bridge, <strong>Ms. Manager LuvJones</strong> flew me out to rock shows in Chicago when nobody in Seattle would put a brotha on. Damn, has it really been seven years?<br />
<br />
It was these excursions into the underground Chicago hip-hop scene from
2000-2003 that I saw folks holding their own on stage, on the page and
building together. It&#39;ll be good to be back.<br />
<br />
So if you dig our shit, do yourself a favor and check our fam in Chicago. You can start with The Pacifics&#39; <em><strong>The Case EP</strong></em>, produced entirely by <strong>Illmind</strong> (Pinoy beatmaker extraordinaire!).<br />
<br />
<strong>STOP THE KILLINGS TOUR<br />
feat. Geologic of Blue Scholars<br />
</strong><br />
MARCH 13<br />
CHICAGO, IL<br />
@ Subterranean (21+)<br />
2011 W North Ave.<br />
<br />
MARCH 14<br />
MILWAUKEE, WI<br />
@ Club Timbuktu (21+)<br />
520 E Center St.<br />
<br />
MARCH 16<br />
NEW YORK, NY<br />
@ Club M1-5<br />
52 Walker St.<br />
<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-03-12 | Monday</font></strong><br><br>don&#39;t hate the playa, hate the littering people that throw beer cans and garbage all over la playa to make it dirty.<br /><br />last saturday, i went to see my buddy <strong>Hari</strong> open up for <strong>Zach Galifinakis</strong> at the <strong>Moore Theater</strong>.  in spite of a few borderline jokes that would have made <strong>daps1</strong> exclaim the infamous explicative &quot;that&#39;s racist!&quot; the show overall was quite hilarious.<br /><br />&quot;look, i make fun of racism because it&#39;s funny, not because i agree with it.  i don&#39;t wanna see any frat boys comin to high five me after the show.&quot; -ZG<br /><br />the good news for today is, the new <strong>Limited Artist Edition Shirt</strong> is done.  this installment&#39;s designer is <strong>ONESEVENNINE</strong>.  for those of you at the <strong>Vera Project&#39;s</strong> opening show, you might have noticed a display of her work on the wall.  we like her.  so we demand that you do too.<br /><br /><img src="http://www.bluescholars.com/images/hangar.jpg" alt="" /><br /><br />above is an image of a mural she did by the Hangar Cafe.<br /><br />the shirt will be available sometime toward the end of April and zapmama is it gonna be filth.<br /><br />saba<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=190">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]